.TH TIROK 1 "2026" "tirok" "Portfolio Management Tool"
.SH NAME
tirok \- portfolio management CLI and TUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tirok
.br
.B tirok
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tirok
is the terminal management tool for the TIROK portfolio site.
Run it with no arguments to open the interactive full-screen TUI,
or pass a command for one-shot use from scripts and your shell history.
.PP
It talks directly to the SQLite database
.RI ( site.db )
inside the Docker volume and wraps
.B docker compose
for service control \(em no HTTP session or browser required.
.SH TUI
Launching
.B tirok
with no arguments opens a curses-based menu. Navigate with the arrow keys or
.BR j / k ,
select with
.BR Enter ,
and go back with
.BR Esc
or
.BR q .
.PP
Submenus are available for Posts and Projects. Any operation that needs
terminal interaction (writing content, confirming a deletion, tailing logs)
drops out of the TUI cleanly and returns to the menu when done.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Posts
.TP
.B tirok post ls
List all posts. Output columns: id, status, title, slug. Newest first.
.TP
.B tirok post add
Interactive mode. Prompts for title, slug, category, tags, cover image, and
status, then opens
.B $EDITOR
for the Markdown content.
.TP
.BI "tirok post add \-\-json " FILE
Non-interactive. Reads post data from a JSON file.
.I FILE
may contain a single post object or a JSON array for bulk import.
.TP
.BI "tirok post edit " "id|slug"
Re-opens the interactive editor with current values pre-filled.
Accepts a numeric id or the post slug.
.TP
.BI "tirok post rm " "id|slug"
Prompts for confirmation, then permanently deletes the post, its tags,
and its comments.
.TP
.BI "tirok post import " FILE
Alias for
.BI "tirok post add \-\-json " FILE \fR.
.TP
.B tirok post export
.TQ
.BI "tirok post export " FILE
Dump all posts (including content and tags) to JSON.
Prints to stdout if no path is given.
.SS Projects
.TP
.B tirok project ls
List all projects. Output columns: id, status, featured flag, name, GitHub URL.
.TP
.B tirok project add
.TQ
.BI "tirok project add \-\-json " FILE
Add a project. Interactive or JSON-driven (single object or array).
.TP
.BI "tirok project edit " id
Re-open the interactive editor for an existing project.
.TP
.BI "tirok project rm " id
Delete a project after confirmation.
.TP
.BI "tirok project import " FILE
Alias for
.BI "tirok project add \-\-json " FILE \fR.
.SS Service control
.TP
.B tirok start
.TQ
.B tirok stop
.TQ
.B tirok restart
Pass-through to
.B docker compose start / stop / restart
using the compose file at
.RI $ TIROK_DIR /docker-compose.yml
(default:
.IR /opt/portfolio/docker-compose.yml ).
.SS Logs
.TP
.B tirok logs
.TQ
.BI "tirok logs \-n " N
.TQ
.B tirok logs \-f
.TQ
.BI "tirok logs \-n " N " \-f"
Show container logs.
.B \-n
sets the number of tail lines (default: 80).
.B \-f
streams new log lines live; press Ctrl-C to stop.
.SS Status
.TP
.B tirok status
Print the Docker container state, database path, backup count in
.IR /var/backups/tirok/ ,
total posts (published vs draft), and project count.
.SS Backup
.TP
.B tirok backup
Zip
.I site.db
and the
.I uploads/
directory from the Docker volume into
.IR /var/backups/tirok/tirok_backup_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.zip .
Automatically prunes to keep the 10 most recent backups. Also called
automatically before
.B update
and
.BR uninstall .
.SS Restore
.TP
.B tirok restore
.TQ
.BI "tirok restore " FILE
With no argument, lists all backups in
.I /var/backups/tirok/
and prompts for a selection. With a path, restores that specific zip directly.
.PP
The restore sequence: stop the service \(-> overwrite
.I site.db
and
.I uploads/
in the Docker volume \(-> restart the service.
.SS Update
.TP
.B tirok update
Create a backup, run
.B git pull origin main
inside the install directory, then
.B docker compose up \-d \-\-build
to rebuild and restart the container.
.SS Uninstall
.TP
.B tirok uninstall
Prompts for
.I yes
confirmation, then: creates a final backup, runs
.B docker compose down \-v
(removes containers and the data volume), removes the Nginx site config,
removes
.IR /opt/portfolio ,
and removes
.IR /usr/local/bin/tirok .
Backups in
.I /var/backups/tirok/
are
.B not
deleted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the command reference and exit.
.TP
.BR \-n " " \fIN\fR ", " \-\-lines " " \fIN\fR
(logs only) Number of log lines to tail. Default: 80.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-follow
(logs only) Stream log output live.
.TP
.BR \-\-json " " \fIFILE\fR
(post add, project add) Read data from a JSON file instead of interactive prompts.
.SH JSON SCHEMAS
.SS Post
.nf
{
  "title":      "My Post Title",        \fR(required)\fP
  "content":    "# Heading\\n\\nBody.",  \fR(required, Markdown)\fP
  "slug":       "my-post-title",        \fR(auto if omitted)\fP
  "excerpt":    "Short summary.",       \fR(auto if omitted)\fP
  "category":   "Dev",                  \fR(created if new)\fP
  "tags":       ["go", "backend"],      \fR(created if new)\fP
  "coverImage": "https://\&.../cover.jpg", \fR(https:// or /uploads/)\fP
  "status":     "draft"                 \fR("draft" or "published")\fP
}
.fi
.SS Project
.nf
{
  "name":        "calcirok",             \fR(required)\fP
  "description": "Kernel calculator.",   \fR(required)\fP
  "github":      "https://github.com/\&...", \fR(required)\fP
  "stack":       ["C++", "Linux"],
  "status":      "wip",                  \fR("active" | "wip" | "archived")\fP
  "featured":    true,
  "sortOrder":   0
}
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TIROK_DIR
Install directory containing
.IR docker-compose.yml .
Default:
.IR /opt/portfolio .
.TP
.B EDITOR
Text editor opened for post and project content. Default:
.BR nano .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/tirok
The installed CLI wrapper.
.TP
.I /opt/portfolio/scripts/cli/tirok.py
The Python script invoked by the wrapper.
.TP
.I /opt/portfolio/docker-compose.yml
Docker Compose configuration used for service control.
.TP
.I /var/lib/docker/volumes/portfolio_portfolio-data/_data/site.db
SQLite database accessed directly by the CLI.
.TP
.I /var/backups/tirok/
Backup destination. Zip files named
.IR tirok_backup_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.zip .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Open the interactive TUI:
.RS
.B tirok
.RE
.PP
Quick status check:
.RS
.B tirok status
.RE
.PP
Write a post in vim:
.RS
.B EDITOR=vim tirok post add
.RE
.PP
Seed multiple projects from a JSON file:
.RS
.B tirok project add \-\-json seed-projects.json
.RE
.PP
Export all posts before migrating:
.RS
.B tirok post export backup-posts.json
.RE
.PP
Tail live logs while debugging:
.RS
.B tirok logs \-n 200 \-f
.RE
.PP
Snapshot data before making changes:
.RS
.B tirok backup
.RE
.PP
Roll back to a previous backup interactively:
.RS
.B tirok restore
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker-compose (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1),
.BR nano (1)
.PP
Full documentation:
.I /opt/portfolio/docs/CLI.md
